# FRONTEND.md — Flutter + Riverpod Implementation Guide (Design + Flows)

## 0) Non-negotiable approach
- The Figma file is messy: do NOT try to generate production code by mirroring each “state screen”.
- Build a clean code design system in Flutter first, then implement screens by composition.
- Recitation and Quiz must be single “engines” driven by state, not dozens of duplicated widgets.

## 1) Stack
- Flutter
- Riverpod (state management)
- go_router (routing)
- supabase_flutter (auth/db/storage)
- record + just_audio (recording/playback)
- permission_handler
- freezed/json_serializable (models)

## 2) Design tokens (from design system reference)
### Colors
- Primary CTA gradient: #1DCFEB → #5BA9FF
- Progress active: #FF9D00
- Progress track:  #4F5457
- Gamification light: #E7EBEF
- Success: #03BF35
- Danger:  #EC6361
- Warning: #FFD500
- Neutral gray: #3D3D3D
- Black: #000000
- White: #FFFFFF
- Text muted: #687D91
- Text navy:  #042748

### Shadows/accents (used as “depth” cues)
- Stable button accent: #05B734 / #E88F00 / #0086FF
- Action inner shadow: #A8F2BC / #AED2F3 / #F3EBAB

### Spacing + radii (choose and enforce)
- Spacing scale: 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24 / 32
- Radius: 12–18 for buttons/cards (consistent)
- Illustration slot on learning screens: reserve ~35–45% of vertical space

## 3) Core reusable components (must implement first)
1) PrimaryButton (variants: primary, success, warning, danger, disabled, loading)
2) ActionIconButton (square + round; inner shadow variants)
3) ModalSheet (success/fail/info; supports illustration slot)
4) ProgressBar + StarsRow (simple, no heavy stats top bar early)
5) QuizOptionCard (default/selected/correct/wrong/disabled)
6) RecorderModule (idle → recording → review → submitting)
7) RewardCard (Hasanat/badge/trophy)
8) StatTile (streak/time/score)
9) IllustrationFrame (forces consistent image sizing)

## 4) Navigation + screen responsibilities (MVP)
Auth/Parent:
- Splash/Onboarding (optional)
- SignIn / SignUp / OTP / VerifySuccess
- SetPin / EnterPin
- SelectChild
- AddChild
- ParentDashboard (later in MVP)
- ParentSettings (later in MVP)

Child:
- ChildHome (journey/path)
- SurahOverview
- AyahLearn (illustration + meaning + listen)
- RecitationPractice (engine screen)
- QuizScreen (engine screen; supports quiz types)
- ProgressHome (links to Streak/Time/Score)
- StreakScreen
- ReciteTimeScreen
- ScoreScreen

Rule: Keep “RecitationPractice” and “QuizScreen” as single screens driven by state.

## 5) Riverpod state model (minimal)
Global:
- authSessionProvider
- parentProfileProvider
- selectedChildProvider

Feature providers:
- childSettingsProvider(childId)
- surahProgressProvider(childId, surahId)
- ayahProgressProvider(childId, surahId, ayahId)
- recitationControllerProvider(params)  // state machine driver
- quizControllerProvider(params)

Repository pattern:
- SupabaseClient wrapper
- ProgressRepository (reads progress, subscribes if needed)
- RecitationRepository (upload audio + call edge function)
- QuizRepository (submit quiz)

## 6) Frontend state machines (must mirror backend)
### RecitationPractice screen
States:
- Idle
- Recording
- Reviewing (playback)
- Submitting (upload/call)
- FeedbackSuccess / FeedbackFail
- InterventionRequired (after 2 consecutive fails)
- LockedOut (daily cap)
- GateToQuiz (mini/final)
- AyahMastered (when passesRequired met)

UI is driven entirely by the backend response from recitation_submit:
- passesRemaining
- attemptsLeftToday
- showDetailedFeedback
- mustReplayLearnStep
- shouldBlurVerse
- nextGate
- locked_until

### QuizScreen
Supports quiz types:
- mini_1, mini_2, final
Question variants (UI templates):
- recite-from-memory prompt
- fill in blank / continuation
- match meanings
- comprehension MCQ

Quiz order is enforced by backend stage.

## 7) How to use Figma efficiently (without cleanup)
Use Figma for:
- token confirmation (colors, gradients, radii)
- reference layouts for key screens (golden path)
- illustration sizing expectations

Do NOT:
- generate 1:1 screen code for every “start-XX” state
- mirror group/rectangle layer names in Flutter

Recommended input method:
- Put reference screenshots (golden path) in /design/key_screens
- Put sticky rules in /design/sticky_notes
- Treat /docs/*.md as the true spec

## 8) Build order (Codex-friendly)
1) Theme tokens + component library (PrimaryButton, ModalSheet, RecorderModule, QuizOptionCard)
2) Router skeleton + placeholders
3) Supabase auth screens + parent gate + child selection
4) Surah/Ayah content screens
5) Recitation engine (record/upload/submit/display results)
6) Quiz engine + gates
7) Progress dashboards

## 9) UI/UX constraints from project notes
- Illustrations must be large and comfortable—use IllustrationFrame and reserve space.
- Avoid heavy stats top bar early in quiz flows.
- Pathway visuals can be simplified; avoid repeating galaxy motif everywhere.
- Mini quiz schedule is fixed: after 2 verses, mini quiz; total 2 minis then final exam.
- Failure logic should feel encouraging but strict (backend-enforced caps and intervention).
